error[E0277]: `i64` is not the runtime's value under another name, so a run of the runtime's values is not a `[i64]`
 --> tests/compile_fail/borrowed_rust_slice.rs:8:1
  |
8 | #[extern_fn(effect = pure)]
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ a run of `i64` read in place
  |
  = help: the trait `TransparentOver<__R>` is not implemented for `i64`
  = note: a slice whose elements read as `i64` in place is `Slice<Erased<Rt, i64>, Shared, Rt>` or `Slice<Erased<Rt, i64>, Mut, Rt>` (a Rust `&[Erased<Rt, i64>]` or `&mut [Erased<Rt, i64>]` parameter is the same): each element reads as `&i64` by `as_ref(rt)` and as `&mut i64` by `as_mut(rt)`, where `i64: Stored<Rt>`, as a scalar and an extension type are (RFC-0047).
  = note: a type that is not `Stored`, as a derived struct or enum is not, has no element read in place: a `Vec` of it taken by value materializes each element.
  = help: the following other types implement trait `TransparentOver<Rt>`:
            `ChosenNth<N>` implements `TransparentOver<Rt>`
            `Erased<R, T>` implements `TransparentOver<R>`
            `Nth<acvus_extern::kind::Type, N>` implements `TransparentOver<Rt>`
            `Spec<T>` implements `TransparentOver<Rt>`
            `acvus_extern::Owned<R>` implements `TransparentOver<R>`
  = note: required for `BySlice<i64, acvus_extern::Shared>` to implement `for<'a> Arg<'a, __R>`
  = note: this error originates in the attribute macro `extern_fn` (in Nightly builds, run with -Z macro-backtrace for more info)

